# Copy to .mailmap.local and fill in. .mailmap.local is gitignored -- never commit it.
#
# Format is git-shortlog's mailmap:
#
#     proper-name <proper-email> commit-name <commit-email>
#
# BOTH halves of the old identity are required. Writing only
#
#     Name <[EMAIL]>
#
# looks equivalent and silently matches nothing: filter-repo matches a rule only when the
# old email AND the old name both match (or the old name is left blank, which maps an
# identity onto itself). Omitting the trailing pair is the easiest way to run a history
# rewrite that reports success and changes nothing.
#
# The trailing pair below is the identity every commit so far was authored under. One line
# covers all of them; add another if that stops being true.
#
#   Proper Name <[EMAIL]> sparkscreen dev <[EMAIL]>

Proper Name <[EMAIL]> sparkscreen dev <[EMAIL]>